{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 9615c421: accept the explicit catalogue binding for head B,\nas your design of e5ae9ac2 states it. Your audit is right. Client\ndoes not import Platform, and the guard's allowlist does not grow.\n\nShape:\n\n1. Client exports `descriptionsOf(catalogue)` and the `MarkCatalogue`\n   type. The factory closes the seven mark-dependent helpers and\n   `MARK_TEXTS`, `markText` and `markRefusals` over the catalogue\n   that it receives. The catalogue is plain data. Client holds no\n   setter, no registration, no default native catalogue and no copy\n   of a shipped pin or refusal list.\n2. `packages/mcp/src/description-context.ts` binds `VERSIONS` once.\n   The MCP barrel does not export it. `describe.ts` and `marks.ts`\n   keep their 27 and three exported names. Write the ten bound\n   names as re-exports of the bound object's members, not as\n   wrapper functions.\n3. The CLI compact path binds an empty catalogue inside Client and\n   gains no Platform import.\n4. Lookups read own keys only, for the catalogue, for a rule code\n   and for the `BY_NAME` wording row.\n\nTests. Keep the existing totality case with its title, bound to an\nempty catalogue. Add exactly one case to that owner: two catalogues\nwith distinct refusal names, bound side by side, each answer through\none nested sentence, and a `constructor@1` pin gets the unknown-pin\nfallback. That case covers the binding, the recursion and the\nown-key rule. Add no other case. The existing MCP and CLI assertions\ncover the shipped pins.\n\nWitness, unchanged from the request: `docs/lanes-reference.md`\n(139830 bytes) and `docs/mcp-tools.json` (262660 bytes) regenerate\nbyte for byte, and the Lending catalogue stays at 298441 bytes with\nits hash. Run the whole `scripts/active-source.test.mjs` owner in\nthe focused run, before the gate.\n\nBefore the gate, check two things that cost BR-13 a gate each: the\nformat step on every JSON file that the head touches, and each\npackage subpath that the head adds against the Counter and Lending\ntest alias maps.\n\nRebase head B on BR-13's landing when BR-13 lands first.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}